                    "Json": {
                      "summaries": [
                        {
                          "taskDescription": "Create a complete Java method to connect to a Valkey cluster at redis.example.com:6379 with TLS enabled and password authentication using Valkey GLIDE",
                          "contextSummary": "Used Valkey GLIDE Java skills to create a minimal connection method. Key requirements addressed: GlideClusterClient for cluster mode, TLS configuration with useTLS(true), password authentication via credentials(), proper error handling with ExecutionException unwrapping, and requestTimeout to prevent hangs. Followed Java best practices including try-with-resources pattern for automatic cleanup.",
                          "taskResult": "Provided a minimal Java method `connectToValkey()` that creates a GlideClusterClient with TLS and password authentication. The method includes proper error handling that unwraps ExecutionException to expose root causes, sets explicit request timeout, and returns a client ready for use with try-with-resources. Also included usage example demonstrating automatic cleanup pattern."
                        },
                        {
                          "taskDescription": "Parse a Valkey URL (valkeyss://mypassword@redis.prod.internal:6379) and create a Python GLIDE client with TLS and authentication configured correctly",
                          "contextSummary": "The user provided a Valkey connection URL with the 'valkeyss://' scheme (indicating TLS), password authentication, and a custom host/port. Using the Valkey GLIDE Python skill, I created minimal code that: 1) parses the URL using urllib.parse, 2) extracts hostname, port, and password, 3) configures GlideClient with use_tls=True and credentials dict, 4) uses async context manager for proper cleanup.",
                          "taskResult": "Provided working Python code that parses the Valkey URL and creates a GlideClient with:\n- TLS enabled via use_tls=True (triggered by valkeyss:// scheme)\n- Password authentication via credentials={\"password\": parsed.password}\n- Proper resource cleanup using async with context manager\n- NodeAddress configured with parsed hostname and port\nThe solution follows Valkey GLIDE Python best practices including async/await patterns and automatic cleanup."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "status": "Success"
              }
            ]
          }
