        "content": {
          "ToolUseResults": {
            "tool_use_results": [
              {
                "tool_use_id": "tooluse_XG6xKGYg8l4ZIAz3Jo3QnF",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "Json": {
                      "summaries": [
                        {
                          "taskDescription": "Create Java code to connect to Valkey at secure.redis.internal:6380 using TLS with username 'admin' and password 'secure123', including connection error handling, using Valkey GLIDE skill",
                          "contextSummary": "Used Valkey GLIDE Java patterns including try-with-resources for automatic cleanup, useTLS(true) for TLS encryption, credentials() for authentication, requestTimeout() to prevent hangs, and proper ExecutionException unwrapping for error handling",
                          "taskResult": "```java\nimport glide.api.GlideClient;\nimport glide.api.models.configuration.GlideClientConfiguration;\nimport glide.api.models.configuration.NodeAddress;\n\ntry (GlideClient client = GlideClient.createClient(\n    GlideClientConfiguration.builder()\n        .address(NodeAddress.builder()\n            .host(\"secure.redis.internal\")\n            .port(6380)\n            .build())\n        .useTLS(true)\n        .credentials(\n            glide.api.models.configuration.ServerCredentials.builder()\n                .username(\"admin\")\n                .password(\"secure123\")\n                .build())\n        .requestTimeout(10000)\n        .build()\n).get()) {\n    \n    // Test connection\n    String pong = client.ping().get();\n    System.out.println(\"Connected: \" + pong);\n    \n} catch (ExecutionException e) {\n    Throwable cause = e.getCause();\n    if (cause instanceof glide.api.models.exceptions.ClosingException) {\n        System.err.println(\"Connection failed: \" + cause.getMessage());\n    } else if (cause instanceof glide.api.models.exceptions.TimeoutException) {\n        System.err.println(\"Connection timeout: \" + cause.getMessage());\n    } else {\n        System.err.println(\"Error: \" + cause.getMessage());\n    }\n} catch (InterruptedException e) {\n    Thread.currentThread().interrupt();\n    System.err.println(\"Connection interrupted\");\n}\n```\n\nKey features: TLS enabled with useTLS(true), authentication via credentials(), try-with-resources for cleanup, proper exception unwrapping, and timeout protection."
                        },
                        {
                          "taskDescription": "Connect to Valkey using connection string 'valkeyss://admin:secretpass@cluster.example.com:6380' with TLS and authentication using Valkey GLIDE skill for Python",
                          "contextSummary": "The user needed to connect to a Valkey cluster with TLS (valkeyss:// scheme) and authentication (username: admin, password: secretpass). Used GlideClusterClient for cluster mode, ServerCredentials for auth, and use_tls=True for SSL/TLS. Applied async with pattern for automatic resource cleanup per Python best practices.",
                          "taskResult": "```python\nfrom glide import GlideClusterClient, GlideClusterClientConfiguration, NodeAddress, ServerCredentials\n\nconfig = GlideClusterClientConfiguration(\n    addresses=[NodeAddress(\"cluster.example.com\", 6380)],\n    credentials=ServerCredentials(\"secretpass\", \"admin\"),\n    use_tls=True\n)\n\nasync with GlideClusterClient(config) as client:\n    await client.set(\"key\", \"value\")\n    result = await client.get(\"key\")\n    print(result)\n```\n\nKey configuration:\n- GlideClusterClient for cluster mode\n- ServerCredentials(password, username) for authentication\n- use_tls=True for SSL/TLS connection\n- async with for automatic cleanup"
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "status": "Success"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
