              "args": {
                "command": "create",
                "file_text": "# TLS and Authentication Validation Results\n\n**Date:** 2026-03-12  \n**Purpose:** Validate that consolidated TLS/auth reference files work correctly for Java and Python\n\n## Test Results: ✅ 4/4 PASSED\n\n### Java Tests\n\n#### Test 1: TLS + Password Authentication (Cluster)\n**Prompt:** Connect to redis.example.com:6379 with TLS and password 'mySecretPassword'\n\n**Result:** ✅ PASS\n- ✅ Used `GlideClusterClientConfiguration.builder()`\n- ✅ Called `useTls(true)`\n- ✅ Used `ServerCredentials` with password\n- ✅ Used try-with-resources\n- ✅ Handled `ExecutionException` with `.getCause()`\n\n#### Test 2: TLS + Username + Password (Standalone)\n**Prompt:** Connect to secure.redis.internal:6380 with username 'admin' and password 'secure123'\n\n**Result:** ✅ PASS\n- ✅ Used `ServerCredentials.builder()` with both username and password\n- ✅ Called `useTLS(true)`\n- ✅ Unwrapped `ExecutionException` with `getCause()`\n- ✅ Used try-with-resources\n- ✅ Set explicit `requestTimeout(10000)`\n\n### Python Tests\n\n#### Test 3: Parse valkeyss:// URL with Password\n**Prompt:** Parse `valkeyss://mypassword@redis.prod.internal:6379` and create client\n\n**Result:** ✅ PASS\n- ✅ Parsed URL to extract TLS flag from `valkeyss://` protocol\n- ✅ Extracted password from URL\n- ✅ Used `ServerCredentials` (credentials dict)\n- ✅ Set `use_tls=True` in config\n- ✅ Used `async with` context manager\n\n#### Test 4: Parse valkeyss:// URL with Username + Password (Cluster)\n**Prompt:** Parse `valkeyss://admin:secretpass@cluster.example.com:6380` and create cluster client\n\n**Result:** ✅ PASS\n- ✅ Parsed URL to extract username and password\n- ✅ Detected TLS from `valkeyss://` protocol\n- ✅ Used `ServerCredentials(password, username)` with both parameters\n- ✅ Set `use_tls=True`\n- ✅ Used `GlideClusterClient` for cluster mode\n- ✅ Proper async error handling with context manager\n\n## Key Findings\n\n### What Worked\n1. **Consolidated reference files are effective** - AI correctly found and used TLS/auth documentation\n2. **Java patterns are solid** - ServerCredentials, useTls(), try-with-resources all generated correctly\n3. **Python URL parsing works** - AI correctly detected `valkeyss://` protocol and extracted credentials\n4. **Fresh agents succeed** - No subagent context issues when using fresh agents\n\n### Code Quality\n- All generated code follows language-specific best practices\n- Proper resource cleanup (try-with-resources, async with)\n- Correct error handling patterns\n- Appropriate client selection (GlideClient vs GlideClusterClient)\n\n## Conclusion\n\n✅ **TLS and authentication documentation is working correctly** after consolidation into reference files. Both Java and Python skills successfully guide AI to generate correct, production-ready code for secure Valkey connections.\n\nThe previous hour-long hang was due to attempting to use a non-existent \"skill-testing\" skill. Using fresh subagents with direct prompts works perfectly.\n",
                "path": "glide-workspace/tls-auth-validation/VALIDATION_SUMMARY.md",
                "summary": "Document TLS/auth validation results"
              },
