  "latest_summary": [
    "## CONVERSATION SUMMARY\n* Validated Valkey GLIDE skill across 6 programming languages (Python, Java, Go, C#, PHP, Node.js)\n* Discovered Python-specific issue where AI generates incorrect `client.ft_search()` syntax instead of correct `ft.search(client, ...)` module-level functions\n* Attempted 7 iterations to fix Python issue with increasingly explicit documentation, warnings, and API references\n* Updated `python-parse-valkey-urls.md` to reflect new URL parsing that extracts TLS and credentials (5 return values instead of 2)\n* Created test script to verify URL parsing with TLS and password authentication\n* Discovered validation methodology flaw: subagents consistently generate incorrect Python code, but fresh agents with same skill generate correct code\n* Indicates issue is with subagent context passing, not the skill itself\n* Verified Git commit 0f5c341 simplified Markdown links correctly - all file references are valid\n\n## TOOLS EXECUTED\n* Read skill-creator methodology from `/opt/dev/oss/skills/skills/skill-creator/SKILL.md`\n* Examined Python validation results across iterations 1-6 in `glide-workspace/python-iteration-*/`\n* Checked Git diff for langchain-aws valkey.py showing new URL parsing implementation\n* Created and ran `test_url_parsing.py` to test URL parsing with ports 6380, 6480, 6479\n* Spawned subagents for validation testing across all 6 languages\n* Verified file existence for all language-specific references (java, go, csharp, nodejs, php, python)\n* Checked Git commit 0f5c341 for simplified Markdown link changes\n\n## CODE AND TECHNICAL INFORMATION\n* Updated `_parse_valkey_url()` function signature: returns `tuple[str, int, bool, str | None, str | None]` (host, port, use_tls, username, password)\n* URL parsing now extracts TLS from protocol suffix \"ss\" (valkeyss://, rediss://)\n* Extracts credentials from URL format: `valkeyss://:password@host:port` or `valkeyss://username:password@host:port`\n* Python FT API uses module-level functions: `ft.create(client, ...)`, `ft.search(client, ...)`, `ft.dropindex(client, ...)`\n* Redis-py uses different pattern: `client.ft().search()` which causes AI confusion\n* Test results: Java (✅), Go (✅), C#(✅), PHP (✅), Node.js (✅), Python (❌ in subagents, ✅ in fresh agents)\n* Created comprehensive API reference in `references/python-ft-api.md` with examples and explanations\n* Drafted GitHub issue `ISSUE-python-search-api-generation.md` documenting the problem\n\n## KEY INSIGHTS\n* Validation methodology using subagents is flawed - subagents don't receive full skill context properly\n* Python skill actually works correctly when tested with fresh agents (not subagents)\n* Type-safe languages (Java, Go, C#) prevent API hallucinations through compiler enforcement\n* Dynamic languages without Redis-py confusion (PHP, Node.js) also work correctly\n* The documented \"Python limitation\" is actually a testing artifact, not a real skill limitation\n* Success rate is likely 100% (6/6 languages), not 83% (5/6) as previously concluded\n* Skill-creator methodology emphasizes \"explain the why\" and \"lead with examples\" but this didn't resolve subagent issue\n* All file references in Git commit 0f5c341 are valid and correctly point to existing files\n\n## TODO ID\n* None\n\n## FACTUAL RECORD\n\n### Files Modified and Read\n_(Showing 30 of 79 files, most frequently and recently accessed first. Writes weighted 2x more than reads. Indented items show summaries for the last 5 modifications.)_\n* references/python.md (13 modifications, 16 reads, showing summaries for last 5 modifications)\n  - Add client.ft_search() and client.ft_create() pitfalls to Common Pitfalls table\n  - Add prominent vector search API example at top of file\n  - Add reference to new FT API document\n  - Remove redundant VECTOR SEARCH API section, keep prominent link to API doc\n  - Add critical warnings section at top of python.md\n* test_url_parsing.py (5 modifications)\n  - Create test for URL parsing with TLS and password\n  - Fix test to accept empty string for username\n  - Change test to use port 6480\n  - Add actual connection test to verify TLS and credentials work\n  - Change port to 6479\n* references/python-anti-patterns.md (3 modifications, 4 reads)\n  - Add binary data decoding anti-pattern to Python anti-patterns document\n  - Simplify binary data anti-pattern and reference decode docs\n  - Remove moved sections from anti-patterns file\n* references/python-ft-api.md (3 modifications)\n  - Create terse FT module API reference from source code\n  - Expand FT API reference with more examples and explicit warnings\n  - Restructure API doc to lead with why and complete example\n* ISSUE-python-search-api-generation.md (2 modifications)\n  - Draft GitHub issue for Python Search module API generation problem\n  - Convert file references to relative Markdown links\n* glide-workspace/python-iteration-5/REVIEW_SUMMARY.md - Create Python iteration 5 summary with recommendation\n* references/python-parse-valkey-urls.md - Update URL parsing to include TLS and credentials extraction\n* /home/jonathan/Work/Repos/AWS/valkey-glide/python/glide-sync/glide_sync/sync_commands/ft.py\n* evals/evals.json - Create comprehensive Python-focused test cases targeting documented anti-patterns\n* glide-workspace/nodejs-iteration-1/REVIEW_SUMMARY.md - Create Node.js iteration 1 summary\n* evals/evals-nodejs.json - Create Node.js-specific test cases\n* glide-workspace/php-iteration-1/REVIEW_SUMMARY.md - Create PHP iteration 1 summary\n* evals/evals-php.json - Create PHP-specific test cases\n* glide-workspace/csharp-iteration-1/REVIEW_SUMMARY.md - Create C# iteration 1 summary\n* evals/evals-csharp.json - Create C#-specific test cases\n* glide-workspace/go-iteration-1/REVIEW_SUMMARY.md - Create Go iteration 1 summary\n* evals/evals-go.json - Create Go-specific test cases\n* glide-workspace/java-iteration-1/REVIEW_SUMMARY.md - Create Java iteration 1 summary\n* evals/evals-java.json - Create Java-specific test cases\n* glide-workspace/iteration-3/REVIEW_SUMMARY.md - Create iteration 3 summary\n* glide-workspace/iteration-2/REVIEW_SUMMARY.md - Create iteration 2 summary\n* glide-workspace/iteration-1/REVIEW_SUMMARY.md - Create review summary for human evaluation\n* glide-workspace/iteration-1/benchmark.json - Create benchmark placeholder\n* glide-workspace/grade_outputs.py - Create grading script for automated assertion checking\n* glide-workspace/iteration-1/session-manager/eval_metadata.json - Create eval metadata for test 8\n* glide-workspace/iteration-1/cluster-batch/eval_metadata.json - Create eval metadata for test 7\n* glide-workspace/iteration-1/create-index/eval_metadata.json - Create eval metadata for test 6\n* glide-workspace/iteration-1/mock-testing/eval_metadata.json - Create eval metadata for test 5\n* glide-workspace/iteration-1/code-review/eval_metadata.json - Create eval metadata for test 4\n* glide-workspace/iteration-1/batch-fetch-sync/eval_metadata.json - Create eval metadata for test 3\n\n### Commands Executed\n_(Showing 20 of 30 commands, most frequently and recently executed first)_\n* cd /home/jonathan/Work/Repos/AWS/Valkey-Samples/skills/glide && python3 test_url_parsing.py - Run test with port 6479\n* cd /home/jonathan/Work/Repos/AWS/Valkey-Samples/skills/glide && \\\necho \"=== Checking all referenced files ===\" && \\\nfor file in \\\n  references/java-pa... - Verify all language-specific file references\n* cd /home/jonathan/Work/Repos/AWS/Valkey-Samples/skills/glide && \\\nfor lang in java go csharp nodejs php; do\n  echo \"=== Checking references/${lang}.md... - Check file references in other language files\n* cd /home/jonathan/Work/Repos/AWS/Valkey-Samples/skills/glide/references && \\\necho \"Checking references/python.md links:\" && \\\nfor file in python-ft-ap... - Verify all file references in python.md\n* cd /home/jonathan/Work/Repos/AWS/Valkey-Samples/skills/glide/references && \\\ngrep -oE '\\[[^]]+\\]\\(